extraction_notes: |
  - Read from the OCR cache of a scan and verified line by line against 200 dpi
    renders of printed 27 and 28. The entry starts in the left column of 27,
    below the First Stage Promethean''s last line, and ends at the top of 28 with
    Money and Cybernetics.
  - IT IS AN O.C.C., AND ITS OWN BOOK CONTRADICTS ITSELF ABOUT THAT. Printed 26
    refers the reader to the "Promethean Phase Adept R.C.C." in the middle of
    the First Stage Promethean''s Phase Powers paragraph; the heading on printed
    27 reads "Promethean Phase Adept O.C.C." Settled the way the Naruni Repo-Bot
    was settled in #415 - from the FIELDS, not from a heading and not from an
    index. This entry prints Attribute Requirements, O.C.C. Abilities and
    Bonuses, O.C.C. Skills, O.C.C. Related Skills, Secondary Skills, Standard
    Equipment, Money and Cybernetics, and NO Attributes line, where every R.C.C.
    in this book rolls eight. Every field says occupation. Imported as occ.
  - THE PHASE POWERS ARE CATALOGUED, AS PSIONIC POWERS IN A NEW CATEGORY. The
    book''s own first sentence on printed 32 is "Phase powers seem to be a
    variation on psionic abilities. Like psionic powers, they are activated by
    using I.S.P.", and each of the fifteen prints Range, Duration, I.S.P. and a
    description - the exact column set psionic_powers holds. The category select
    in js/catalog-fields.js carries allowOther with a comment saying a later
    book may add a category the core four do not cover, so Phase costs no code
    change. The gate is safe in both directions: psiConfig in app.js defaults a
    class stating no categories_allowed to the core four rather than to
    "anything", so no published class can reach a Phase power, and the eight
    psionic classes that state no categories_allowed were checked one by one -
    none has a powers_schedule or a powers_per_level, so none has a level-up
    picker to leak through either.
  - THE SURVEY SAID THESE POWERS WERE THE SECOND STAGE PROMETHEAN''S AND THAT IS
    WRONG. Printed 32 says outright that besides prometheans only the phase
    mystic O.C.C. can learn them; this class takes six at first level and one
    per level after, and the phase mystic takes four and one per level. They are
    not one NPC''s racial abilities.
  - THE MASTER TIER IS INHERITED, NOT PRINTED ON THIS ENTRY. Printed 27-28 does
    not contain the word master anywhere: the First Stage Promethean''s block on
    printed 26 says "Considered a master psionic" and the Phase Mystic''s on
    printed 29 says "They are considered to be master psionics", and this entry
    says only "in addition to the normal psionic powers available to all
    prometheans". A phase adept IS a first stage promethean, and this entry
    grants a super-psionic power at first level, which in Palladium only a
    master psychic may take - so master is what the tier has to be. Recorded
    because it is an inference from two printed facts rather than a third
    printed fact, which is a different thing and the reconcile pass was right to
    separate them.
  - THIS CLASS''S PSIONICS ARE DISCARDED WHEN IT IS PLAYED ON ITS OWN RACE, WHICH
    IS THE ONLY WAY THE BOOK ALLOWS IT TO BE PLAYED. combineClasses in
    js/parser.js keeps whichever psionics block is STRICTLY the higher tier, so
    the First Stage Promethean''s block stays and all six phase powers, the
    super-psionic pick and the twenty-eight schedule entries above are dropped.
    Measured against the real parser, not reasoned about. THE TIER ABOVE IS NOT
    WHAT CAUSES THIS and lowering it would not help: master is the top of the
    ladder, the race holds it, and the comparison is strict, so this block loses
    at every tier it could carry. Filed as BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F10. Nothing
    about this class is written down differently because of it: the block is
    what the book prints, and the finding is where the gap is recorded.
  - The race''s four automatic powers - empathy, telepathy, total recall and mind
    block auto-defense - are NOT repeated here. This entry says "in addition to
    the normal psionic powers available to all prometheans" and lists none of
    them, unlike the Noro Psychic in #409, whose own entry does list the race''s
    five. What the entry prints is what is stored.
  - THE +1D6 P.S. AND +1D4 P.P. ARE STORED AS DICE, NOT DROPPED. The Apok''s note
    says bonuses.attributes takes flat numbers only; that has not been true
    since the Godling''s +1D4 initiative, and validateBonusGroup in js/parser.js
    accepts a dice expression in every group. Checked before writing them.
  - Standard Equipment: the steelcloth robes are A.R. 12 and 90 M.D.C., read off
    the render, and are added to the gear catalog by this batch - the book names
    and stats them, which is more than the plasma hand cannon had in #415. The
    "suit of heavy environmental body armor (150 M.D.C.)" is NOT made a row: the
    book names no item, only a class of armor and a figure, so it is a choice
    among the armors this book does stat, and the printed 150 is recorded here.
    The heaviest of those is the CAF Heavy Battle Armor at 120 M.D.C.
  - Money: 2D6x1000 in credit or trade items, read on printed 28. Note that the
    Promethean Time Master''s Money line is 2D6x1000 as well and the Phase
    Mystic''s is 2D4x1000; printed 29 carries two complete Standard Equipment /
    Money / Cybernetics triples, one at the top and one at the bottom, so each
    was read off the render rather than off a field-source window.
