## Lore

The phase adepts are first stage prometheans who have dedicated themselves to
the mastery of phase powers for the protection of their race. They are the
equivalent of mystic warriors, with an arsenal of exotic abilities built out of
their phase nature: they walk through walls, make their bodies intangible, alter
the weight and momentum of objects, and teleport in combat. Their teachings
include a strict code of honor and an oath to protect Phase World, and other
worlds, from invaders and despoilers.

Most adepts are on Phase World, guarding key installations and enforcing the law
at Center - at least in the areas that remain under promethean control. At some
point, though, every adept is expected to leave for a while, anything from
decades to centuries, and travel the Three Galaxies or the Megaverse to learn
more about the universe and his place in it. Those on such furloughs usually act
as law enforcers, bodyguards or crusaders, and they are among the few beings who
often work alongside cosmo-knights against threats on a cosmic scale.

## GM Notes

Force fields are the standard countermeasure: most phase powers, teleportation
included, will not work through even the flimsiest one. Magic barriers hinder or
stop them too, and most magic spells and weapons do full damage to a first stage
promethean. The book''s own advice is that phase-powered characters belong in
high-powered or cosmic campaigns, and that an adept who abuses the powers draws
bounty hunters, mercenaries, cosmo-knights and other prometheans down on him.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'promethean-phase-adept');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'promethean-phase-adept';
SELECT count(*) AS stub_gear FROM gear WHERE slug IN ('steelcloth-robes', 'meditation-chip');

